enings at the Annecy Animation Film Festival in June 2012.\n\n- Hi no Youjin and Buki yo Saraba are based on Katsuhiro Ootomo's manga of the same name, whereas Tsukumo and Gambo are original stories."},"tags":[{"name":"Anthology","rank":100,"spoiler":false},{"name":"CGI","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Historical","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Post-Apocalyptic","rank":73,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Full CGI","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Demons","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Military","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Gore","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Desert","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Samurai","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Nudity","rank":30,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"SHORT PEACE","english":"SHORT PEACE","native":"SHORT PEACE","romaji":"SHORT PEACE","synonyms":[{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"短暂和平"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"ショート・ピース"}]},"trailer":{"id":"x1SVedf4S1g","site":"youtube","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/x1SVedf4S1g/hqdefault.jpg"},"visibility":"general"}